Actual Weil explicit-formula convention adapter

This standalone package is released under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
It reuses the zeta23 formalization from anthropics/formal-math at commit
fbdc36bbf17d20af3fd0447c6d1a8a02773c9844 through a pinned Git dependency.
The upstream proof sources are not vendored in this package.

Zeta23: Copyright 2026 Anthropic, PBC; Apache License, Version 2.0.
The mathematics formalized there is attributed to Levent Alpöge and Ralph
Furman, “More than two thirds of the zeta zeros are simple and on the
critical line,” arXiv:2608.13637. The upstream project attributes its Lean
code to Claude (Anthropic), with the paper authors directing and reviewing
the formalization and Eric Easley orchestrating it.

The pinned Zeta23 checkout's NOTICE identifies the files under
`Zeta23/FromPNTPlus/` adapted from PrimeNumberTheoremAnd, Copyright the
PrimeNumberTheoremAnd contributors; Apache License, Version 2.0. The checkout
also preserves applicable Mathlib source notices. Lake fetches the remaining
dependencies as separate packages; this integration does not vendor their
source trees. See the pinned dependency for their individual notices and
licences.

The convention adapter in ActualWeil.lean is an additional wrapper. It does
not claim a new explicit formula, zero-proportion theorem, or RH proof.
